<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<odoo>

    <template
        id="software_workflow_dec.mail_notification_layout"
        inherit_id="software_license_pass.mail_notification_layout"
    >
        <xpath expr="//div[@name='extra']" position="inside">
            <h1>Documentation</h1>
            <p>
                All software and hardware manuals and user guides will be available in the DEC e-space.
            </p>
            <h1>DEC e-space</h1>
            <p>
                All your licences, subscriptions and applications are managed via the new <b
                >« DEC e-space »</b> launcher. You can find the software and documentation at this address :
            </p>
            <a
                class="action-link"
                href="https://public-support.decgroupe.com/launcher-v2/launcher_classic.exe"
            >Download our launcher</a>
            <p>
                The DEC e-space software user guide is freely available at :
            </p>
            <a
                class="action-link"
                href="https://vr.docs.decgroupe.com/applications/launcher-userguide"
            >Read the user guide</a>

            <p class="figure alert alert-info">
                <small>
                    The simplified use of this application requires access to the <t
                        t-esc="object.user_id.company_id.portal_name"
                    /> in the form of an account (e-mail and password). See below.
                </small>
            </p>

            <h1> <t t-esc="object.user_id.company_id.portal_name" /> </h1>
            <p>
                <img
                    src="/portal_workflow_dec/static/img/portal_access_sample.jpg"
                    style="width:30%;height:30%;"
                />
            </p>
            <p class="figure alert alert-info">
                <small>
                If you did not previously have access to the portal, then you should have received a second email, entitled <i
                    >« Your access to <t
                            t-esc="object.user_id.company_id.portal_name"
                        /> »</i>, which asks you to create activate your account.
                </small>
            </p>
            <p>
                Our portal allows you to view your orders and invoices, as well as manage your licenses and subscriptions or those of your establishment. You can also create a support ticket for an after-sales service request.
            </p>
            <p class="figure alert alert-success">
                To delegate the management of your licenses and subscriptions, you can use the following link to access a form that allows you to create an account for each of your collaborators, which will be attached to your organization. (as a child of your account: <t
                    t-esc="record.partner_contact_id and record.partner_contact_id.name"
                />).
            </p>
            <p>
                <a
                    t-att-href="record and record.partner_contact_id and record.partner_contact_id.get_delegate_signup_url()"
                >
                    <t
                        t-esc="record and record.partner_contact_id and record.partner_contact_id.get_delegate_signup_url()"
                    />
                </a>
            </p>
            <p class="figure alert alert-danger">
                Please note that you must not share this link with the public!
            </p>
            <!--
            <p>
                You can find the various documents at the following addresses:
            </p>
            <p>
                TODO: Generate list of resources fron linked apps
            </p>
            <h1>General information</h1>
            <p class="figure alert alert-success">
                If your system computer hasn't been turned on for a long time, don't
                forget to update Windows and Oculus/Vive depending on your hardware.
            </p>
            -->
        </xpath>
    </template>

    <template
        id="software_workflow_dec.view_email_template_pass_send"
        inherit_id="software_license_pass.view_email_template_pass_send"
    >

        <xpath expr="//p[@name='contact']" position="inside">
            <t
                t-if="object.partner_contact_id.unfenced_commercial_partner_id and object.partner_contact_id.unfenced_commercial_partner_id != object.partner_contact_id"
            >
                (<t
                    t-esc="object.partner_contact_id.unfenced_commercial_partner_id.name"
                />)
            </t>
        </xpath>

    </template>

</odoo>
